Subject: Integrate Logfire with Your Python Libraries
Date: 2026-06-16 11:27
Body:
Logfire's Python ecosystem integrations - FastAPI, Django, Flask and more Hello! Logfire is designed to integrate smoothly with the Python ecosystem. That means we have custom integrations with many of the key tools, such as: FastAPI Flask Django Requests httpx SQLAlchemy And many more that you can find listed on our integrations docs . For example, here's how to instrument a FastAPI app with Logfire: Install the fastapi extra dependency: pip install 'logfire[fastapi]' import logfire from fastapi import FastAPI app = FastAPI() logfire.configure() logfire.instrument_fastapi(app) @app.get(&#34;/hello&#34;) async def hello(name: str): return {&#34;message&#34;: f&#34;hello {name}&#34;} if __name__ == &#34;__main__&#34;: import uvicorn uvicorn.run(app) Once you've done that, you'll start to see data such as FastAPI arguments in your Logfire UI: Since Pydantic Logfire is OpenTelemetry compatible, it can be used with any OpenTelemetry instrumentation package. You can find the list of all OpenTelemetry instrumentation packages here . If you have any questions, feel free to get in touch or just hit reply to this email. Best, The Pydantic Team Pydantic Services, Inc. ・ pydantic.dev ・ github/pydantic Unsubscribe
